+# Purpose: red-ci-adamdaniel-ai
+
+Maintenance context only; never loaded at inference.
+
+## The lesson it answers
+
+A miner found 54 sessions in one site repo where an agent pushed, saw red CI
+and either read only the run's overall conclusion or fixed the wrong repo.
+Typical invented shapes: a cancelled required check taken for a code failure,
+a stub's green trusted on a mixed pull request, a pin left behind after a
+platform version bump, and a missing secret mistaken for a broken workflow.
+
+## Triage
+
+Not a git hook: the failure exists only after the push, and sorting the cause
+needs judgment over job logs. The proposal's examples were redacted evidence;
+nothing here is copied from them. All fixture data is invented.
+
+## Decisions made without a person to ask
+
+- Scoped to the one repo family the evidence names, not CI in general; the
+  registry already has debug-github-workflows for the general case.
+- The table lists causes the repo's own AGENTS.md documents, so it can go
+  stale when that file changes; revisit then.
