+---
+name: red-ci-adamdaniel-ai
+description: Triage red or blocked CI on a pull request in a Jekyll/Decap consumer site repo whose machinery lives in a platform repo (adamdaniel.ai and cms-platform). Use when a push or PR shows a failing, cancelled or never-reporting check, a BLOCKED PR with green checks, a pin-consistency failure, or a scheduled workflow failing at setup. Read the failing JOBS, name the cause, and fix it in the repo that owns it.
+---
+
+# Red CI in a platform-consumer site repo
+
+The site repo holds content, identity and thin workflow callers. The machinery
+(reusable workflows, the e2e harness, the admin UI, the pin checks) lives in
+the platform repo and arrives by a pinned version. So a red check is usually
+one of six causes, and the fix often belongs in the other repo.
+
+## 1. Read the jobs, not the run
+
+A run's conclusion hides which job went red. List the run's jobs and steps
+(`gh run view <id> --json jobs`) and name the first failed job and step. Then
+read that job's log. Report what you parsed, never what a watch command's exit
+code suggested.
+
+## 2. Sort the cause
+
+| What the job shows | Cause | Fix |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cancelled` on a required check, a newer run exists for the same head | superseded run, or a `timeout-minutes` wall (GitHub reports a timeout as `cancelled`) | Re-run that one job; do not edit code. A cancelled required context blocks the merge until a success replaces it. |
+| Green `e2e / e2e` on a PR that also touched code paths | the instant-green stub satisfied the context before the real run reported | Treat green as unverified; wait for the real run to finish. |
+| Pin-consistency job lists a reference at an old version | the platform version is named in many places and one was left behind | Bump every reference together with the platform-bump flow; never edit one pin by hand. |
+| Failure at `Set up job`, or a missing secret or variable message | environment: a secret or repo variable is unset or expired | Name the secret or variable for the owner to set. Do not change the workflow or skip the leg. |
+| PR `BLOCKED`, every check green | the branch is behind its base, or a required context is not published | Update the branch from its base and wait for the checks to re-run; confirm the required context is one something emits. |
+| A test fails on a platform-owned file (admin UI, harness, theme) | the defect is in the platform repo | Change it there and ship a release; the site repo only bumps the pin afterwards. |
+
+## 3. Rules that hold
+
+- Never skip, disable or quarantine a test to turn a check green.
+- Never push an empty commit or close and reopen a PR to kick CI.
+- Do not re-vendor platform files into the site repo.
+- A 404 from GitHub on a private repo means "not visible to this token".
+- Say which jobs you read and which you could not.
+
+## 4. Write the triage down
+
+When asked for a triage, give: the failing job and step by name, the cause
+class from the table, the one action that fixes it, and the repo that owns the
+fix. Keep it to those four things.
